# DAW Timeline Rules

## Component Hierarchy

```
DAWDock.tsx                  ← bottom-docked shell: state, gestures, context menu, connection lines
  ├─ DAWToolbar.tsx          ← transport, timecode, snap select, zoom, export dropdown, bake banner
  ├─ DAWRuler.tsx            ← adaptive tick ladder, click-to-seek, drag = loop region, double-click loop = remove
  ├─ DAWTrackHead.tsx        ← per-track: color badge, name, sub-label, M/S, fader, kebab menu
  ├─ DAWLane.tsx             ← per-track clip lane (grid background, overlap detection)
  │    └─ DAWClip.tsx        ← one clip block (cached-peaks canvas, name label, badges, edge trim handles)
  ├─ DAWClipMenu.tsx         ← right-click context menu (variant / linked-entity override, reset clip trim)
  └─ DAWBarControls.tsx      ← snap / zoom % / export, portaled by DAWDock into SceneBottomBar (right of "Timeline") while expanded; dock height auto-fits up to 1/3 of the window, manual drag up to 1/2
                                (no transport — play/stop live in the scene bottom bar)
```

Supporting hooks/utils, all in `frontend/src/components/audio/daw/`:
`useDawView.ts` (zoom / snap mode / dock height — see "Zoom Auto-Fit" below), `useClipSelection.ts` (click / ctrl / shift / marquee
selection), `useClipGesture.ts` (drag, group drag, duplicate — one store commit per gesture),
`useClipTrimGesture.ts` (per-clip edge trim + reset), `daw-trim.ts` (pure trim math),
`daw-snap.ts` (pure snap resolution: off / 0.1 / 0.5 / 1 / smart + edge magnetism).

Kept unchanged: `DAWMiniTransport.tsx` (compact bar shown when the dock is collapsed),
`DAWTransportBtn.tsx`, `frontend/src/lib/audio/peaks-cache.ts`.

A clip's identity is `clipKey = ${soundId}-${originalIterationIndex}` — do not parse it, only
construct/compare it.

## Zoom Auto-Fit (first open) vs. Manual Zoom

`DAWDock` unmounts when collapsed, so zoom cannot live in component state. `useDawView` derives it:
`pxPerSecond = uiStore.timelineView.pxPerSecond ?? fit`, `trackHeight = timelineView.trackHeight ?? fit`.

- **Horizontal fit** = `(viewport − left/right insets − HEAD_WIDTH − FIT_SCROLLBAR_ALLOWANCE) / duration`, so the
  whole timeline fills the dock width. Derived from `window.innerWidth` + the dock insets — never from a DOM
  measurement (the dock's `transition-all` animates its width, which would make a measured fit lag/jitter).
- **Vertical fit** = `TRACK_HEIGHT` lowered by `FIT_TRACK_HEIGHT_NOTCHES` (2) wheel-out notches (`WHEEL_ZOOM_OUT`).
- Any manual change (Ctrl/Alt+wheel, status-bar ±) writes `timelineView` (per axis), which then wins over the
  fit — collapsing and re-expanding restores the user's zoom. `null` on an axis = auto-fit again.
- `timelineView` is session-local (excluded from `partialize`); dock height/`autoFit` are persisted separately.

## No Lock Toggle — Every Track Is Draggable

The old interval/timestamps lock button is gone. A track with no `soundTimestamps` entry is "auto"
(its clips are derived from the interval default). Dragging, trimming or deleting one of its clips
first freezes the displayed positions into an explicit schedule via `ensureTrackMaterialized()`
(exported from `useClipGesture.ts`). The track head shows a small `auto` chip while a track is
still auto.

## Per-Clip Trim (edge drag)

Each clip's left/right edge can be dragged to trim that one iteration (`useClipTrimGesture.ts`).

- **Storage:** `audioControlsStore.iterationTrims[clipKey] = { start, end }` — fractions (0–1) of the
  clip's *variant* source buffer. A clip trim **overrides** the variant's card trim
  (`soundTrims[variantSoundId]`); clips without one follow the card trim.
- **One resolver:** `resolveIterationTrim()` (`lib/audio/utils/iteration-trim.ts`) is used by the DAW
  drawing (`timeline-utils`), live playback (`build-score`) and WAV export — never read
  `soundTrims` directly for a clip.
- **Anchored audio:** a left-edge trim moves the clip start with the trim start (one
  `setIterationTrim(…, newStartSec)` commit = one undo entry) and clears that clip's orchestrate
  trigger, like a manual drag. A right-edge trim only changes the end.
- **Ripple:** `setIterationTrim` re-bakes; the solver's `iterationDurations` makes `after()` /
  `alignEnd()` dependents and same-track serialization follow the trimmed length.
- **Keys move with clips:** `iterationTrims` uses the same keys as `iterationLinks`, so every
  insert/remove must remap both (`remapIterationKeys` in `lib/audio/utils/iteration-keys.ts`).
  Duplicate/paste pass `readClipTrimCopy()` to `remapIterationLinksForInsert` so the copy keeps the
  trim (and its variant). Changing a clip's variant drops its trim. Resetting a track to auto drops them too.
- Persisted: undo history, localStorage, and `soundscape.json` (`iteration_trims`).

## Waveform Rendering — Cached Peaks, No WaveSurfer in the Dock

`DAWClip` draws from `peaks-cache.ts` (`getAudioPeaks`) onto a plain `<canvas>` — it never mounts a
WaveSurfer instance. This is a static thumbnail only; it never plays audio. WaveSurfer is still used
elsewhere for `WaveSurferPlayer.tsx` / `SoundCardWaveSurfer.tsx` sidebar cards.

## Playback Sync

`DAWDock` receives `currentTime`/`isPlaying` from `SceneTimeline` → `SpeckleScene`'s playback state,
plus an optional `playbackSchedulerRef` (`PlaybackSchedulerService`) for future ref-driven playhead
updates. `Transport`/`playback-scheduler-service.ts` are never modified by DAW UI work.

## audioControlsStore — Playback Control State

Single source of truth for all runtime playback state. Import from `@/store` barrel.

| Field | Type | Purpose |
| ----- | ---- | ------- |
| `soundVolumes` | `Record<soundId, number>` | Per-sound volume, dBFS |
| `soundTimestamps` | `Record<soundId, number[]>` | Explicit clip start times (seconds); no entry = auto track |
| `mutedSounds` | `Set<soundId>` | Muted sound IDs |
| `soloedSounds` | `Set<soundId>` | Every variant id of each soloed track (multi-solo; empty = none). Resolve audibility with `isSoundSilenced` (`lib/audio/utils/mute-solo.ts`) |
| `iterationLinks` | `Record<clipKey, IterationLink>` | Per-clip variant/entity overrides |
| `iterationTrims` | `Record<clipKey, TrimRange>` | Per-clip trim overrides (see Per-Clip Trim) |
| `timelineDurationMs` | `number` | Total timeline length in milliseconds |

`handleTimestampsChange`/`handleTimestampsChangeBatch` never sort — free drag and overlap are safe.
Use the batch variant so one drag/nudge/delete-multi is as few undo entries as possible.

## Export Formats

`frontend/src/lib/audio/SoundscapeExporter.ts` handles all export formats (mono / binaural / FOA /
TOA), exposed via the export dropdown in `DAWToolbar.tsx`.

## Adding New DAW Features

| Feature type | Where to edit |
| ------------ | ------------- |
| Per-track UI (mute/solo/fader/kebab) | `DAWTrackHead.tsx` |
| Per-clip visual | `DAWClip.tsx` |
| Drag / trim / snap / selection behaviour | `useClipGesture.ts`, `useClipTrimGesture.ts`, `useClipSelection.ts`, `daw-snap.ts`, `daw-trim.ts` — do not split gesture math across components |
| Global control (transport, zoom, export) | `DAWToolbar.tsx` + new field in `audioControlsStore` if it's persisted state |
| New export format | `SoundscapeExporter.ts` + expose option in `DAWToolbar.tsx` |

